# Corpus and labels -- fetched, not authored. The Kaggle competition ran 1 Apr - 1 Jul
# 2026 and its terms for redistributing the labelled findings are not stated anywhere
# we could find, so the CSVs stay local and README documents how to fetch them.
# data/splits.json is ours and is tracked: it holds only repository hashes, no labels,
# and reproducing any measurement requires the exact partition.
data/*.zip
data/*.csv
data/ex/

# Upstream Bastet is cloned, not vendored. Our additions to it are mirrored into
# bastet-cc/scripts/ so they are versioned without carrying someone else's tree.
upstream-bastet/

# Secrets. The AIS3 gateway token is issued per team and belongs in the environment.
.env
*.cookies
**/kaggle.json

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Raw per-call transcripts: they embed contract source and prompts verbatim, and grow
# with every run. The derived measurements beside them are what the writeup cites.
# Leading **/ matters -- a bare `runs/` anchors to the repository root and silently
# misses bastet-cc/runs/, which is where these actually live.
**/runs/**/llm_log.jsonl
**/runs/**/llm_calls.jsonl
**/runs/**/results.jsonl
**/runs/**/tasks.jsonl

# Foundry build artefacts from running the probes and the local demo in-tree.
arbiter/cache/
arbiter/out/
